WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.370
- Smile.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.278
- [Mark] So, Reilly, you're back again.

00:00:06.278 --> 00:00:07.220
- [Reilly] I'm back again.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.500
- Or Russia, isn't it?

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.970
Everyone calls you Russia on the street.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:12.200
- [Reilly] They didn't understand that,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.450
that Reilly wasn't a
Russian name (chuckles).

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:16.783
- [Mark] I call you Reilly,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.780
which is actually your last name, right?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.613
- Yeah.

00:00:18.613 --> 00:00:19.542
That's what I like.

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:21.559
- [Mark] Okay, I remember I asked you

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:22.970
what your name was and
what do they call you,

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.862
you said Reilly, so that's what stuck.

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:25.708
- Right.

00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.491
- [Mark] So, what's going on, please?

00:00:28.491 --> 00:00:30.780
- Oh, well, I've got a million stories.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.788
- [Mark] I know you do.

00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:34.700
- I'll forget them because I have PTSD

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.830
and all of a sudden something

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.430
will make me remember something.

00:00:38.528 --> 00:00:39.980
You know, I can't put them
in chronological order,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.330
I can't remember when they happened.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.513
This one happened when I was young.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.520
I can't remember where the hotel is at.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.780
But anyway, I was working at a dance club

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.395
and I was living in one of those hotels

00:00:54.395 --> 00:00:56.789
where nobody talks, everything's,

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.789
nothing's seen, nothing's heard.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:00.210
- [Mark] Yes.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.342
- And next door to me was this man

00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:05.650
and then his two children.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.870
One was he said 17, I doubt it.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.400
And the other one was six.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.840
And two girls, there were two girls.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.500
And he was one of these men

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.247
that had that schlurpy Jheri curl

00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:22.247
with all the juicy dripping,
gold teeth in the mouth.

00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:24.318
He was a pimp.

00:01:24.318 --> 00:01:25.570
'Cause he kept trying to get at me

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.653
and I'd be like, kind of a hostile guy.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.595
And then one day, I was
getting off the elevator

00:01:32.595 --> 00:01:34.260
and maybe you have to understand,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.523
I have molestation issues.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.400
I'm not able to just let things pass by

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.090
when I see other children or kids

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.390
and things happen to them.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.810
So, I got in this elevator

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.648
and I stepped off and there
was nobody left, right,

00:01:50.648 --> 00:01:53.803
at the exit of the elevator.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.560
But then I heard like crying.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.230
And I turned around and back in the day,

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.660
they had those kind of trash cans,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.680
they were kind of a dome

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.151
and the top was like a little ash tray.

00:02:03.151 --> 00:02:05.885
And I looked behind it and
there's this little girl

00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:07.620
who's six years old, my neighbor.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.620
And she's crying and she
has blood all in her,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.440
she had these little shorts on.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.460
And I said, "What happened?"

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.300
And she said, "No, no, no."

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.993
And I said, "Baby, you
want me to get your dad?"

00:02:21.993 --> 00:02:23.723
"No, no, don't get him, he'll be so mad

00:02:23.723 --> 00:02:27.850
because I made the trick mad."

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.750
And my brain just snapped.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:30.782
Made the trick mad.

00:02:30.782 --> 00:02:31.937
- [Mark] Made the what?

00:02:31.937 --> 00:02:32.935
- [Reilly] Trick mad.

00:02:32.935 --> 00:02:34.050
She made the trick mad.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.190
- [Mark] The trick.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.023
- [Reilly] The trick.

00:02:36.023 --> 00:02:37.970
He had pimped her out to somebody

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.940
and he had, you know, sex with her

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.990
and she was bleeding.

00:02:42.524 --> 00:02:43.357
- [Mark] This is the six-year-old?

00:02:43.357 --> 00:02:45.310
- [Reilly] It was the six-year-old girl.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.997
And I said, "Do you want me to take,

00:02:46.997 --> 00:02:48.317
you can come on over, do you
want me to call your mother?"

00:02:48.317 --> 00:02:49.987
"No, she'll just sell me back."

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.392
So I took her to my room.

00:02:52.392 --> 00:02:54.530
And I just came from, I had gone to this,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:57.270
my friend had a new tanning salon

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.720
in Beverly Hills with
the high-pressure beds

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.590
and I had gotten really crispy work

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.720
and so I'd stopped by a store

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.860
and they had this sale on this,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.310
that I'd never seen before,

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.941
green rubbing alcohol.

00:03:08.941 --> 00:03:11.160
And I was use it to put in my bath water

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.210
to take the sting out out of the sunburn.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.576
And I bought a case, it
was like 39 cents a bottle.

00:03:15.576 --> 00:03:17.283
So, I bought a box of it.

00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:19.540
And I took this little girl to my room

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.820
and I tried to clean
her up in the bathroom

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.260
and I was trying to talk real calm to her

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.150
because she was damaged goods.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.640
She was just six years old.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.720
I mean, how do you? I
know, I was there before.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.380
So, I just knew I couldn't
let that man have her back.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.213
He came later on,

00:03:35.213 --> 00:03:36.890
he pounds on my door.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.514
A neighbor had seen me
take her into my room

00:03:38.514 --> 00:03:43.514
and I had filled up a bucket
with that rubbing alcohol

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.920
and when he pounded on that door,

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:46.967
I knew he was gonna come in there

00:03:46.967 --> 00:03:47.910
and take that little girl from me,

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.090
so I threw that bucket
of rubbing alcohol at him

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:50.923
and I lit it.

00:03:51.852 --> 00:03:53.519
And he was wearing, I
remember he was wearing

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:55.610
a green Puma jogging suit when

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.973
they first started coming out

00:03:56.973 --> 00:03:59.232
and he ran down this hallway on fire.

00:03:59.232 --> 00:04:01.989
And there was all these
big bright green flames

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:04.173
and his hair was plopping off,

00:04:04.173 --> 00:04:06.602
'cause he was on fire and I pulled

00:04:06.602 --> 00:04:08.400
the little girl in the hallway

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.559
and I said, "He will never hurt you again.

00:04:10.559 --> 00:04:12.870
You see, he will never hurt you again."

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.620
And I pulled her back in the room

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.010
and shut the door.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.880
And I called the office and I told them

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.137
that there was a mess in the hallway

00:04:20.137 --> 00:04:21.870
because it was one of those hotels

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.437
where nobody talks and nobody sees.

00:04:25.987 --> 00:04:27.130
And she had an auntie

00:04:28.014 --> 00:04:30.664
and somehow I found how to
get a hold of this auntie.

00:04:31.578 --> 00:04:34.329
And when I called she was just ecstatic

00:04:34.329 --> 00:04:36.059
that I had called.

00:04:36.059 --> 00:04:38.519
She said as soon as she had the money,

00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:40.780
she would send it to me for the ticket

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.310
to send her back.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.270
I said, "Don't worry about
the ticket, I got the ticket.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:45.170
You just have to promise me

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.450
that you will take care of her

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.197
because she's broken."

00:04:49.197 --> 00:04:54.080
She knows that he'll never
come and hurt her again.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.140
I don't even know what
happened to that man.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:55.973
I don't really care.

00:04:55.973 --> 00:04:58.462
I never heard an ambulance, I don't know.

00:04:58.462 --> 00:04:59.295
I don't care.

00:05:00.516 --> 00:05:01.724
But I know that she's okay.

00:05:01.724 --> 00:05:03.910
Her auntie was so happy to get her back.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.160
She told me that her mother
would never touch her.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.010
If her mother even tried,
she said she would kill her.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:12.067
- [Mark] So the man was
a relation to the girl?

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.350
- To the little girl?

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.250
No, he wasn't.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.670
- [Mark] He was just a pimp.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.070
- His mother, back in
the Midwest someplace,

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:22.264
both of the girls were sisters

00:05:22.264 --> 00:05:24.301
and he took them both.

00:05:24.301 --> 00:05:25.554
She gave him some money.

00:05:25.554 --> 00:05:27.325
He gave them some money and he took

00:05:27.325 --> 00:05:29.023
the two little girls.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.320
- [Mark] So...

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.153
- The one, the older one,

00:05:33.153 --> 00:05:34.550
she liked being there I guess or something

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:37.230
or just kind of like that syndrome

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.540
where you're kidnapped and you-

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.703
- [Mark] So she stayed.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.318
- Yeah, she stayed.

00:05:42.318 --> 00:05:44.091
- [Mark] And the mother,
the auntie you were...

00:05:44.091 --> 00:05:45.260
- The auntie.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:47.477
- [Mark] Where was it?

00:05:47.477 --> 00:05:49.223
- She was in Detroit.

00:05:49.223 --> 00:05:50.720
- [Mark] Detroit.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.370
- And I send her back to Detroit.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:55.660
Because I couldn't keep her.

00:05:57.692 --> 00:06:00.611
I'm not capable of being a mother.

00:06:00.611 --> 00:06:02.020
There's too many people who are good

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.033
at being mothers.

00:06:06.729 --> 00:06:08.980
I try, but I just wasn't too good.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:10.700
I knew that I did what I
was I was supposed to do.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:11.877
That's what I was supposed to do.

00:06:11.877 --> 00:06:12.882
I was supposed to save her.

00:06:12.882 --> 00:06:14.180
I was supposed to get her away from there

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.220
and then pass her on to somebody

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.343
who would be good at raising a child.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:19.670
- [Mark] I don't know if a lot of people

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.770
could do what you did.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.993
- I can't think of any other
way I could have done that.

00:06:25.993 --> 00:06:29.729
It was just like, that just seemed like,

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:32.790
I didn't even think about it.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:33.954
Rubbing alcohol was in my hand,

00:06:33.954 --> 00:06:36.903
this man's not gonna get this little girl.

00:06:36.903 --> 00:06:38.160
Whatever I have to do,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.350
this man is not gonna
get this little girl.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:44.140
He's probably wearing that
same green jogging suit.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.008
They'll probably bury him in it if he's...

00:06:47.008 --> 00:06:50.210
I'm not quite sure what
happened to him, I don't care.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.183
But, yeah.

00:06:51.183 --> 00:06:52.600
It make me feel a lot better.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.883
When I put her on the
bed, she started crying.

00:06:58.239 --> 00:07:01.563
Because I seen it in her eyes
finally somebody helped her.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:04.423
I know that feeling

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:07.494
because I just needed to be helped.

00:07:07.494 --> 00:07:08.660
I'm crying.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.100
That's a trigger of mine.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.880
I have a trigger where I start to cry

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.050
if people are still doing something

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.842
that's really bothering me.

00:07:14.842 --> 00:07:16.526
That's a perpetrator.

00:07:16.526 --> 00:07:17.900
If they know that it bother you,

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.140
whatever it is they're doing bothers you,

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:22.420
annoys you, makes you feel uncomfortable,

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.680
but they continue to do it
for their own gratification.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.910
That's a perpetrator.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.320
And there's levels of that

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.837
and there's the extreme.

00:07:28.837 --> 00:07:31.660
I say why do they keep
doing that, I'm crying.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.050
- [Mark] In some ways,
in some way did that

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.513
event heal some of the damage-

00:07:41.513 --> 00:07:42.640
- Yeah, it made me feel,

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.583
it made me feel, yeah.

00:07:44.583 --> 00:07:47.750
- [Mark] Your own pain was
kind of healed by doing that.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.610
- Absolutely.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.160
I can't think of anything.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.650
I couldn't have lived with myself

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:55.690
if I hadn't have done that.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:58.685
That wasn't an option not doing something.

00:07:58.685 --> 00:08:00.073
That wasn't an option.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:02.505
I had to do that.

00:08:02.505 --> 00:08:04.000
Whatever the case may,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.303
as it seemed to be, the
only thing I could think of.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.890
This man, if I opened that door

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:09.933
and hadn't have done something,

00:08:09.933 --> 00:08:10.957
that man would have
taken that child from me.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.100
- [Mark] Oh, of course he would.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.023
- [Reilly] No matter what he had to do

00:08:13.023 --> 00:08:14.307
to make it.

00:08:14.307 --> 00:08:17.640
We were just some kind of a property

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.303
or a commodity.

00:08:20.303 --> 00:08:22.263
- [Mark] Right.

00:08:22.263 --> 00:08:23.096
- [Reilly] Hi.

00:08:23.096 --> 00:08:24.079
- [Mark] Thank you so much

00:08:24.079 --> 00:08:25.675
for yet another great story.

00:08:25.675 --> 00:08:27.127
- When I think of another
one, I'll come back.

00:08:27.127 --> 00:08:28.993
- [Mark] Yeah, you are
welcome here any time.

00:08:28.993 --> 00:08:29.826
- Okay.

00:08:29.826 --> 00:08:31.343
Say bye, say bye Spot.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.333
I'm an auntie.

00:08:33.333 --> 00:08:34.590
I always babysit people's dogs.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.423
I make a good auntie.

00:08:36.423 --> 00:08:37.690
- [Mark] Beautiful dog.

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.663
- [Reilly] Right, okay, are we off?

